# Test: ze show host platform returns runtime-platform capabilities JSON without a daemon
# VALIDATES: offline fallback -- `show host platform` runs the in-process
#            host.DetectPlatform when no daemon is reachable, producing JSON
#            with the always-present type / read-only-root / fd-limit-soft-current
#            fields describing the runtime platform and its capabilities.
# PREVENTS: regressions where show host platform silently requires a daemon,
#           or where the platform JSON drops its canonical kebab-case fields.
# PLATFORM: host inventory probes systemd/gokrazy sockets + getrlimit; the
# darwin detector (platform_other.go) returns ErrUnsupported at build time so
# the underlying feature cannot succeed. Skip on darwin per
# rules/os-specific-tests.md.
option=skip-os:value=darwin
stdin=config:terminator=EOF_CONF
bgp { }
EOF_CONF

cmd=foreground:seq=1:exec=ze show host platform
expect=exit:code=0
expect=stdout:contains="type"
expect=stdout:contains="read-only-root"
expect=stdout:contains="fd-limit-soft-current"
